course: dictionary
lesson: 10627
title: Unforced
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can give you a clue. Un- often means not, so unforced means not forced. Something unforced is done naturally and easily, without effort or pretending. «Her laugh was unforced, and it made the whole class smile.»
explain: In sport, the word means something different. In tennis, an «unforced error» is a mistake a player makes all by themselves. The other player did not make the shot hard. The player just got it wrong.
explain: Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning. If the sentence is about a smile, a laugh or a voice, unforced means natural and easy. If it is about a tennis match, it means a mistake with no help from the other player.
fact: Un- at the start of a word often means not, so unforced means not forced.
fact: «Unforced» means done naturally and easily, not with effort or pretending.
fact: An «unforced error» is a mistake a player makes on their own, not because the opponent made it hard.
fact: Commentators on tennis matches often say «unforced error» when a player misses an easy shot.
fact: A good check is to swap in a simpler meaning: «Her laugh was natural and easy» still makes sense, so unforced fits.
exercise: «His smile was unforced, as if he really was happy.» What does unforced mean here? | Very large and noisy | Sad and tired | Done because someone made him | *Natural and easy, not pretended
exercise: A commentator says, «That was an unforced error by the player.» What does unforced error mean? | A shot the other player made very hard | A winning point scored by luck | *A mistake the player made on their own
exercise: «The unforced laugh filled the room.» Which word tells you the laugh was natural? | *unforced | room | filled | the
test: «The tennis star made an unforced error on an easy shot.» What does this tell you? | She won the point with a clever trick | She hit the ball very hard over the net | *She missed the shot by herself, not because the other player was good | She played a perfect shot that the other player could not reach
test: Which word could replace unforced in «an unforced smile» without changing the meaning? | *natural | angry | forced | loud
exam: Ella says unforced means the same as forced. Why is she wrong? | Forced and unforced both mean hard work | Both words mean the same thing in tennis | Un- means very, so unforced means very forced | *Un- means not, so unforced means not forced
